{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/975808-canon-widderslainte-characters","id":975808,"title":"Canon widderslainte characters?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-24T20:54:23-07:00","id":975808,"title":"Canon widderslainte characters?","content":"Are there any widderslainte NPCs? Also, which do you consider the best books about Nephandi, besides the information on them in M20?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T21:06:48-07:00","id":975814,"title":"","content":"I'm unfamiliar with likely Widderslainte canon NPCs.<br /> <br /> However, for info on Nephandi, the best books to go to would be the &quot;Book of Madness&quot; and &quot;Infernalism: The Path of Screams.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T02:58:33-07:00","id":975894,"title":"","content":"Note that there are two iterations of <i>Book of Madness</i>, though I don't know how the first one differ from the second, if much at all. (Other than the first book having Al-Aswad) Currently there isn't much written about Nephandi all in all. They really need Sect books. And an Aswadim themed world domination board game.<br /> <br /> Here's two Nephandi that didn't make it to the books <a href=\"http://www.allenvarney.com/av_mage.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.allenvarney.com/av_mage.html</a> . I find Mentor's &quot;fake everything&quot; Rotes hilarious. :-P<br /> <br /> Werewolf's <i>Book</i>(s) <i>of the Wyrm </i>can be helpful for the Malfean Nephandi - especially the descriptions of Malfeas and Majelin Incarnas, Banes and Wyrm Cults. The W20 <i>Book of the Wyrm</i> has a Mage (or is he a Sorcerer?) and two corrupted members of the Syndicate on the Board of Directors.<br /> <br /> For Infernal Nephandi I'd recommend Warhammer's Liber Chaotica books - the Slaanesh, the Tzeentch, the Khorne and the Undivided ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 03-12-2018, 06:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T07:53:32-07:00","id":975944,"title":"","content":"There's definite widderslainte NPCs in Dragons of the East, Book of Madness Revised and Fallen Tower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T08:54:21-07:00","id":975961,"title":"","content":"Mercedes/Amanda from the Mage-book Intro fiction fits the bill. At least Amanda might, as Mercedes Fell and Amanda was reborn with her soul &amp;/or Avatar (or soul/Avatar). The while unfinished Amanda cycle is a do-the-impossible tale of an Archmage redeeming a corrupted Avatar (and it's attached mage).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T03:32:43-07:00","id":976445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/975808-canon-widderslainte-characters?p=975961#post975961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mercedes/Amanda from the Mage-book Intro fiction fits the bill. At least Amanda might, as Mercedes Fell and Amanda was reborn with her soul &amp;/or Avatar (or soul/Avatar). The while unfinished Amanda cycle is a do-the-impossible tale of an Archmage redeeming a corrupted Avatar (and it's attached mage).</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand he might have just hunted her down quickly enough that her Avatar wasn't permacorrupted, or he hunted down her Avatar's hosts until it healed itself. Both have been listed as possible ways of dealing with a Widderslainte Avatar. I forget where in the case of the latter, but the former is in the Mage Storyteller's Handbook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T08:43:09-07:00","id":976541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/975808-canon-widderslainte-characters?p=976445#post976445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the other hand he might have just hunted her down quickly enough that her Avatar wasn't permacorrupted, or he hunted down her Avatar's hosts until it healed itself. Both have been listed as possible ways of dealing with a Widderslainte Avatar. I forget where in the case of the latter, but the former is in the Mage Storyteller's Handbook.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact Senex feels he has to TRY to redeem Amanda is almost conclusive evidence she is something of a widderslainte. Mercedes Fell, walked into the Cauls and inverted her Avatar, then died. Amanda is born with her soul which is her Avatar or born with her soul and Awakens with her Avatar. Or some weird intersection of those. <br /> <br /> In which case, a lot of the Amanda Cycle of fiction is the depiction of a widderslainte slowly succumbing to the darkness within, first in ignorance to what's going on, then in full knowledge and struggling against it. All while Senex is trying to fix his &quot;mistake&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T09:53:38-07:00","id":976582,"title":"","content":"Thanks all, for the info! Which book has Amanda's story? Is the intro of M20?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T10:33:05-07:00","id":976605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/975808-canon-widderslainte-characters?p=976541#post976541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The fact Senex feels he has to TRY to redeem Amanda is almost conclusive evidence she is something of a widderslainte. Mercedes Fell, walked into the Cauls and inverted her Avatar, then died. Amanda is born with her soul which is her Avatar or born with her soul and Awakens with her Avatar. Or some weird intersection of those.<br /> <br /> In which case, a lot of the Amanda Cycle of fiction is the depiction of a widderslainte slowly succumbing to the darkness within, first in ignorance to what's going on, then in full knowledge and struggling against it. All while Senex is trying to fix his &quot;mistake&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the very least, it is proof that he isn't sure what he did worked.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/975808-canon-widderslainte-characters?p=976582#post976582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks all, for the info! Which book has Amanda's story? Is the intro of M20?</div> </div> </div> </div>M2nd as I recall. There may have been more in other books, but the story of her finding out about her previous incarnation is there.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T13:08:14-07:00","id":976686,"title":"","content":"A cause of sadness for Brucato was that the author of the Amanda series couldn't winkle out the time to complete the story for inclusion in the book or in the anthology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}